# Keep the build context small — only pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE
# and src/ are needed (see Dockerfile). Everything below is irrelevant.
# NOTE: pyproject.toml declares `readme` and `license-files`, so those two
# files must stay in the context or the metadata build warns (and, from
# setuptools' 2027-02-18 deadline, fails) on the unmatched pattern.
.venv
venv
.git
.github
*.egg-info
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
data
rag-data
certs
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
.env
tests
docs
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
